<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- AJ-E415: the Screen Recording TCC prompt's usage description.
         macOS terminates apps that trigger the prompt without one. -->
    <key>NSScreenCaptureUsageDescription</key>
    <string>AI Juggler mirrors a desktop instance's window inside its panel so you can supervise it without switching apps. Capture is read-only; nothing is recorded or sent anywhere.</string>
    <!-- Fleet (AJ-E7): finding and pairing your other Macs on this network.
         Since macOS 15, mDNS and connections to the local network need the
         Local Network permission; macOS asks for it with this description,
         and without one the access fails silently. NSBonjourServices lists
         the Bonjour service type Fleet advertises and browses, which macOS
         requires for Bonjour use; it's juggler-link's SERVICE_TYPE (a test
         keeps them equal). -->
    <key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
    <string>AI Juggler finds your other Macs running AI Juggler on this network, and talks to the ones you pair, so Fleet can show and move their sessions.</string>
    <key>NSBonjourServices</key>
    <array>
        <string>_aijuggler._tcp</string>
    </array>
    <!-- Jump to a session's window: focus asks System Events to raise it.
         Under the hardened runtime, Apple Events also need the
         com.apple.security.automation.apple-events entitlement
         (entitlements.plist); without both they're denied with no prompt. -->
    <key>NSAppleEventsUsageDescription</key>
    <string>AI Juggler asks System Events to bring a session's window to the front when you jump to it. It doesn't control other apps otherwise.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
